# React Turborepo Rule

- Keep workspace boundaries clear: deployable apps in `apps/*`, reusable code in `packages/*`.
- Put cross-app primitives in packages (`ui`, `types`, `hooks`, `utils`, `auth-*`), not copied into apps.
- Keep package public APIs explicit via `src/index.ts`; import from package entrypoints, not internal file paths.
- Add or update `build`, `dev`, `typecheck`, and `clean` scripts per package/app so Turbo task graph remains valid.
- Respect Turbo pipeline semantics: cache build/typecheck tasks; keep `dev` persistent and non-cached.
- Avoid circular dependencies between packages; prefer one-way dependency flow from apps -> packages.
- Share env/config through dedicated config packages and typed env helpers; avoid duplicated env parsing.
- Keep TypeScript strictness aligned across apps/packages; centralize common tsconfig options where possible.
- For micro-frontend style apps, keep route/module registration in host modules and domain logic inside each app.
- Changes in shared packages must include quick smoke checks in at least one consuming app.

## Turbo Checklist

- New shared logic belongs in `packages/*`.
- App-specific logic belongs in `apps/<app-name>/src`.
- Exported package APIs are documented by `index.ts`.
- `turbo run typecheck` succeeds after changes.
